hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1365","Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abdullah bin Raja told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sulaym bin Abdul Saluli, He said: We were with Saeed bin Al-Aas in Tabaristan, and a group of the Prophet’s companions, may God bless him and grant him peace, was with him. He said to them: Which of you testified with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the prayer of fear? Then Hudhayfah said: “I am, order your companions to stand up in two groups, one group of them facing the enemy, and one group of them behind you, so you say ‘Allahu Akbar’.” And they all say “Allahu Akbar”, then you bow and they all kneel, then you rise and they all rise, then you prostrate and the group next to you prostrates, and the group stands up. The other is in the face of the enemy, so when you raise your head, those next to you stand up and the others fall down in prostration, then you kneel and they all kneel, then you prostrate and prostrate again. The group next to you, and the other group is standing facing the enemy, so when you raise your head from prostration, those facing the enemy prostrate, then you salute. And you will command your companions if a disturbance attacks them, for it is lawful for them to fight and to speak.”"
